      "id": "injury-report-s1-w20",
      "type": "feature",
      "author": "tessa-wren",
      "title": "Jenings and Flock add new absences before the conference championships",
      "dek": "Mt. Silver’s receiver is listed for six weeks, Mossdeep’s corner for two and Foo Warner for one; the full availability comparison follows.",
      "teams": [],
      "body": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Mt. Silver has two new positive-week injury entries after its 21–14 win over Blackthorn. Gregar Jenings is listed for six weeks and Foo Warner for one. Gregar caught one pass for twenty-five yards in the game. The injury record does not identify the play on which either injury occurred, so the reception and its ensuing fumble should not be treated as a confirmed injury sequence."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Mossdeep's Marshall Flock is listed for two weeks after the 40–3 win over Dewford. The Eclipse already have Poury Holt at four. Flock's absence changes the available defensive group for the Sunyshore rematch; no replacement assignment is established by the current report. A dominant divisional performance and a new availability concern can both be part of the same week's assessment."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Mt. Silver's continuing positive counters include Ariados at eight, Vibrava and Tony Gyarzalez at three, Josh Alakazam and Medicham at two, and Tic Thorpe at one. The Reds advanced with Crem Ftzpatrik at quarterback and contributions from several available receivers. Gregar's new entry reduces the receiving options further before facing a Saffron defense that just recorded seven sacks."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Saffron's Emmitt Smoth remains listed for four weeks, one fewer than in the preceding snapshot. Dam Skattebo led the rushing workload against Lavender with ten carries for fifty-one yards. Sunyshore's 88 Special remains at fourteen weeks. Neither reduction should be reported as a newly suffered injury; these are continuing recovery counters attached to existing entries."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Dewford's Excadrill and Jumpluff have new minor entries with zero weeks remaining. Those records do not support inventing a missed game or a questionable designation. The Breakers have been eliminated, but their new entries still belong in the league-wide comparison. The same treatment applies to recovering players on every other eliminated club."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "The table includes every player with an injury entry in either comparison snapshot. A cleared designation, a counter reaching zero and a new zero-week entry are different events and are labeled separately. Reported weeks are the game's current counters, not independently established medical dates. Roster status and actual participation remain separate facts; this report does not automatically assign a cleared player to the next starting lineup."
        },
